# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env* is gitignored except this file.
#
# ⚠ ONLY these three variables may carry a VITE_ prefix.
#
# Vite inlines every VITE_-prefixed variable into the client bundle at build time.
# It is not hidden, not obfuscated, and not recoverable once shipped — it is published.
# There is no such thing as a secret VITE_ variable (security-baseline.md §3.1).
#
# The anon key being public is the whole premise of the model: its safety comes
# entirely from Row Level Security.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=

# The deployed origin, with scheme and no trailing slash — e.g. https://balaiamihan.com
#
# ⚠ REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION, and it fails quietly if you forget. It builds the password-reset
# redirect in src/routes/admin/reset-password.tsx. Unset, that redirect becomes a relative
# path, Supabase rejects it, and the ONLY account-recovery route this product has stops
# working — FR-069g forbids disabling the owner account and there is no second admin.
#
# The value must also be on Supabase's Redirect URLs allowlist as an exact URL. No wildcards:
# a wildcard entry lets any open redirect on the origin carry the recovery token away.
VITE_SITE_URL=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECRETS — Edge Function environment only. Never here, never with a VITE_ prefix,
# never in the client bundle. Listed for reference; set them with
# `supabase secrets set` (security-baseline.md §3.2).
#
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY   bypasses all RLS
#   RESEND_API_KEY
#   RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET
#   TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY
#   RATE_LIMIT_SALT
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LOCAL TOOLING — `pnpm seed` and `pnpm seed:teardown` only.
#
# The seed writes demo data past RLS, so it needs the service role key in your
# own .env.local. This is the ONE place that key belongs outside the Edge
# Function environment, and it is safe here for exactly two reasons:
#
#   1. .env.local is gitignored
#   2. it has NO VITE_ prefix, so Vite never inlines it into the bundle
#
# Prefixing it with VITE_ would publish a key that bypasses every access control
# in the system. Never do that, not even briefly to debug something.
#
# Leave it unset if you are not seeding — nothing else reads it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
